title: Investment Strike
subtitle: German industry is idling...
view-if: (capital_strike_progress >= 10 or budget <= -5) and spd_in_government
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: unemployment_rate += 1.5; workers_spd*= 0.8; new_middle_spd -= 10; old_middle_spd -= 12; unemployed_spd*=0.8; rural_spd -= 10; trust_in_democracy -= 10; capital_strike_seen = 1; cdu_relation -= 10; fdp_relation -= 10; workers_afd += 6; unemployed_afd += 6; new_middle_afd += 8; old_middle_afd += 10; rural_afd += 10; economic_growth -= 2;
tags: event

= Investment Strike

Our policies have angered business more than any government in decades. Investment has collapsed, plants are being run down, and several companies are moving production abroad. Every newspaper and talk show blames us for the crisis.

What can we do?

- @seize
- @capital_controls
- @propaganda
- @nothing

@seize
title: Take public stakes in the plants that are being shut down!
unavailable-subtitle: [? if left_strength <= reformist_strength : The bulk of the party does not support this radical step. ?] [? if judicial_reform < 3 : The courts would strike it down. ?] [? if works_councils < 1 : We need the works councils on our side first. ?]
choose-if: left_strength > reformist_strength and judicial_reform >= 3 and works_councils >= 1
on-arrival: nationalization_progress += 1; firewall_erosion += 4; unemployment_rate -= 0.8; unemployment_rate -= 0.4 if works_councils >= 3; works_program += 1; workers_spd += 8*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 8*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 2; fdp_relation -= 4; workers_afd -= 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_afd -= 6*(1-dissent); left_strength += 15; reformist_dissent += 10; left_dissent -= 10; factory_takeovers += 1; economic_growth += 1;

If business will not invest, the state will. A new public holding takes stakes in the plants that are being closed, and the works councils run them together with the new owners. The opposition calls it the end of the social market economy.


@capital_controls
title: Offer state guarantees to keep the plants open.
choose-if: judicial_reform >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The courts and EU state-aid rules would block this.
on-arrival: unemployment_rate -= 0.5; workers_spd += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 5*(1-dissent); economic_growth += 1; budget -= 1

Federal guarantees and short-time work keep many of the threatened plants open for now. It blunts the worst of the crisis.



@propaganda
title: Launch a campaign blaming the corporations for the crisis.
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: (radio >= 2 or commercialized_media >= 3) and resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if radio < 2 and commercialized_media < 3 : We have not built up our media enough. ?] [? if resources < 1: We do not have enough resources. ?]
on-arrival: workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 6*(1-dissent); trust_in_democracy += 4*(1-dissent); resources -= 1

We use every channel we have to point out that the same companies paid record dividends last year. Because our media work is strong, it partly works: some of the public anger turns towards the corporations and away from us.


@nothing
title: There is nothing we can do.

There is nothing we can do within the law and the EU treaties.
